      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "7cc84a914a139ee22187abe8a6ebb8639f6be60e",
            "subject": "LU-21328 efalnd: Don't use stale rdma desc for 0 size transfers"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-15 07:12:59.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 16:19:15.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20790 efalnd: Repost an Rx when it is freed",
        "message": "LU-20790 efalnd: Repost an Rx when it is freed\n\nEach QP counts its free receive slots in rq_space. kefalnd_free_rx()\nincreases it when a receive buffer is released, and\nkefalnd_refill_rx() posts at most rq_space buffers.\n\nWhen a message arrives, kefalnd_handle_rx() handles it and then\nrefills one buffer, so the buffer is meant to be released first and\nrefilled second. That holds for a regular receive: LNet consumes the\nmessage while it is being handled, the buffer is released, rq_space\ngoes up by one, and the refill reposts that slot. A delayed receive,\ne.g. a message waiting for an MD to be posted or for router buffers,\nbreaks that order. LNet keeps the buffer past the handler, so the\nrefill runs first, finds rq_space at zero and posts nothing. The\nbuffer is released later from another thread, which raises rq_space\nbut posts nothing. From then on each message releases and reposts\nexactly one buffer, so the extra free slot is never filled. Every\ndelayed receive leaves one more slot empty, until the QP has no\nreceive buffers posted and peers stall retrying.\n\nRefill in kefalnd_free_rx() right after the release, so the order\nholds wherever the buffer is released, and drop the refill calls this\nmakes redundant.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nChange-Id: I924474dc09534121e9862837178da669801085f8\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
